WEBVTT

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:29.580
Thank you, Master Xunyu!

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:31.620
You're up early, Cang.

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:34.410
Not as early as you, Master Xunyu.

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:38.500
All this "Master" business is most
unsettling coming from you.

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:41.870
Hmm? Something stinks.

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:46.200
Is it me? But I just changed my clothes...

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:49.370
Cang. Get down, would you?

00:00:49.370 --> 00:00:51.080
Oh! Sure!

00:00:52.250 --> 00:00:53.290
Huh?

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:01.040
I'm sorry--I missed.

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:05.750
No, you didn't. The bullet
got deflected, that's all.

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:07.370
But how?

00:01:07.370 --> 00:01:11.950
I'm betting we're up against
a Huang He Superior Job.

00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:13.370
No biggie.

00:01:13.370 --> 00:01:18.540
I, Eldridge, King of Burglary
and owner of Goblin Street,

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:20.580
will squash 'em but good.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:23.540
Greater Takeover... set.

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:29.620
They'll be within firing range soon...
and that's when I'll use this to take 'em--

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:31.250
Huh?

00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:32.750
He left the cart?

00:01:36.290 --> 00:01:38.040
S-Sir?!

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:42.910
I've...

00:01:42.910 --> 00:01:45.290
...been robbed...

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:48.500
Wha--?

00:01:52.450 --> 00:01:53.540
Huh?!

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:58.620
Too slow.

00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:14.000
Hmph. Perhaps I shouldn't expect
much from the kingdom's Superiors.

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:47.330
Gouz-Maise's Grudge Conversion...

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:50.370
"Chapter 7: Showdown City"

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:50.370
It's pretty handy: It can convert
the negative emotions of living things

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:54.200
into usable MP and SP, too--
not just dead bodies.

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:56.700
Yes, handy.

00:03:56.700 --> 00:04:00.200
I thought Silver's Wind Hoof
just allowed for air travel.

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:04.160
Who knew <i>that</i> would happen when
combined with Grudge Conversion?

00:04:05.250 --> 00:04:10.040
Well, it made a real muddy mess.
Can't use <i>that</i> in town.

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:13.580
No. You'd go right onto the wanted list.

00:04:13.580 --> 00:04:16.950
Hey--can't you give me a turn already?

00:04:16.950 --> 00:04:20.330
We're going to be late for our meetup
with Marie and the others.

00:04:20.330 --> 00:04:26.200
Ray, a man who rushes a woman through
her bath is not long for this world.

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:29.290
To get stronger?

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:37.040
Yes. Please give us tips for getting our revenge
against that Superior Killer someday.

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:39.000
I... see.

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:41.870
I figured since you've been playing
<i>Dendro</i> longer than I have,

00:04:41.870 --> 00:04:43.580
you'd know all about it.

00:04:43.580 --> 00:04:45.330
Oh, I know all <i>kinds</i> of things!

00:04:45.330 --> 00:04:48.200
I've been out of work for over
a year now and playing all that time.

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:50.250
And you're okay with that?

00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:51.580
Ahem!

00:04:51.580 --> 00:04:55.830
What would you say is your weakness, Ray?

00:04:55.830 --> 00:05:02.250
My range is too short, and things get
bad fast when Nemesis's skill fails.

00:05:02.250 --> 00:05:06.660
Those, yes, and your lack of speed or toughness.

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:09.830
So raise your agility or your endurance!

00:05:09.830 --> 00:05:13.000
That's all the advice I can give on the matter.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:16.750
Now hang on a second. That can't be <i>all</i> all!

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:24.950
Well, not <i>all</i> , but you'll need one of
those two if you want to get stronger.

00:05:24.950 --> 00:05:28.200
I can't just specialize in offense,
focus on STR?

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:32.790
You'll die, because you're
neglecting your AGI and END.

00:05:32.790 --> 00:05:37.660
STR is great and all, but if you're slow
and squishy, you'll go down fast.

00:05:37.660 --> 00:05:39.450
So that's how it works...

00:05:39.450 --> 00:05:43.330
Apparently that Superior Killer
has a high-agility Superior Job.

00:05:43.330 --> 00:05:48.540
You'll need to boost those two stats
if you want to stand a chance.

00:05:48.540 --> 00:05:54.700
Your real-life skills--like if you're good at martial
arts or drawing, that'll be reflected here.

00:05:54.700 --> 00:05:58.120
Martial arts, eh? Wonder if
that's true for my brother.

00:05:58.120 --> 00:06:02.580
And then there's your Embryo's ultimate skill.

00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:03.700
Oh?

00:06:03.700 --> 00:06:08.950
This is its mightiest skill,
named after the Embryo itself.

00:06:08.950 --> 00:06:12.200
Without exception, these have powerful effects

00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:15.000
that express the Embryo's
unique characteristics.

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:17.120
So that's "Nemesis" for me.

00:06:17.120 --> 00:06:22.120
Right. But the earliest you can
learn it is after reaching high rank.

00:06:22.120 --> 00:06:27.410
High rank, huh? Wait, have you
already learned your ultimate skill?

00:06:27.410 --> 00:06:30.750
You know, I've never seen your Embryo, Marie.

00:06:30.750 --> 00:06:36.580
Well, my, uh, my Embryo's name is Arc-en-Ciel.

00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:39.290
"Rainbow"! How cool is that?

00:06:39.290 --> 00:06:43.410
And as for what type of Embryo it is, well...

00:06:45.120 --> 00:06:47.660
Sorry we kept you waiting!

00:06:47.660 --> 00:06:49.540
I'm starving!

00:06:49.540 --> 00:06:50.450
Morning, you tw--

00:06:50.450 --> 00:06:54.200
And a very good morning to you, Rook and Babi!

00:06:54.200 --> 00:07:02.200
Hungry, are you? Breakfast is on me!
I'll head up to the counter to order.

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:11.080
These are for you two.

00:07:11.080 --> 00:07:14.870
This is where the rest of that
Gardranda bounty went.

00:07:14.870 --> 00:07:18.790
Clash of the Superiors... with Figaro?

00:07:18.790 --> 00:07:19.830
Against who?

00:07:19.830 --> 00:07:24.450
The player ranked second in Huang He's
duel rankings: Xunyu, the Master Jiangshi.

00:07:24.450 --> 00:07:26.580
I'd love to see that!

00:07:26.580 --> 00:07:31.200
Well, let's split up for now and
meet again at the time on the tickets.

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:32.250
Sure.

00:07:32.250 --> 00:07:34.750
What are your plans in the meantime, Ray?

00:07:34.750 --> 00:07:39.870
I'll hit the Adventurers' Guild
and collect my reward. You?

00:07:39.870 --> 00:07:43.160
I've got to talk to Marie about something.

00:07:43.160 --> 00:07:45.160
You do?

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:48.250
Huh? How'd you--?

00:07:48.250 --> 00:07:49.950
What's up?

00:07:49.950 --> 00:07:51.370
I'm not telling.

00:07:51.370 --> 00:07:53.540
What the heck is going on?

00:07:53.540 --> 00:07:59.950
Eighty million lir for defeating the
Gouz-Maise Gang seems <i>way</i> too high.

00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:03.200
It looks like it was inflated
by some bonus rewards.

00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:08.450
This is far too much to accept alone.
I need to find Hugo.

00:08:08.450 --> 00:08:10.000
Yeah.

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:14.750
I can't even touch these riches
till after I've talked with him.

00:08:20.370 --> 00:08:23.750
Now, now--no pushing, grizz!

00:08:26.620 --> 00:08:27.580
Huh?

00:08:27.580 --> 00:08:29.620
What are you doing, big bro?

00:08:29.620 --> 00:08:33.330
Hmm? If you're calling me
"big bro," you must be...

00:08:33.330 --> 00:08:35.500
Hey! If it isn't Ray, grizz!

00:08:35.500 --> 00:08:38.910
It feels like it's been a while, Brother Bear.

00:08:38.910 --> 00:08:43.290
Okay, kids, it's time for Mister Bear
to get a move on, grizz!

00:08:43.290 --> 00:08:45.200
But before I do...

00:08:45.200 --> 00:08:47.620
Have some candy, grizz!

00:08:50.450 --> 00:08:53.410
Let's pop into a café somewhere, grizz.

00:08:53.410 --> 00:08:55.370
Yeah, let's--

00:08:57.910 --> 00:09:00.950
You, uh, have something on your head.

00:09:00.950 --> 00:09:01.910
I'm sorry.

00:09:01.910 --> 00:09:03.200
Grizz?

00:09:07.410 --> 00:09:10.370
My Behemoth was bothering you.

00:09:10.370 --> 00:09:13.450
Behem--you mean this here?

00:09:13.450 --> 00:09:14.250
Right.

00:09:14.250 --> 00:09:17.790
Hey, your ride's here, little missy! Grizz!

00:09:17.790 --> 00:09:19.410
XD!

00:09:19.410 --> 00:09:22.500
Get down from there. We're leaving.

00:09:27.450 --> 00:09:29.700
If you'll excuse us.

00:09:29.700 --> 00:09:31.790
One sec, grizz.

00:09:34.250 --> 00:09:36.500
A little gift, grizz!

00:09:40.290 --> 00:09:41.700
Thank you very much.

00:09:41.700 --> 00:09:43.410
Thx

00:09:49.450 --> 00:09:51.580
What's wrong?

00:09:51.580 --> 00:09:56.620
I must be imagining things. After all,
she did have her Embryo with her.

00:09:56.620 --> 00:09:59.200
Satisfied, Behemoth?

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:00.540
lol

00:10:00.540 --> 00:10:06.160
Good. I know you said you wanted to hug
that bear because it was so cute.

00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:10.830
I hope you can get what you want
from today's fight, too.

00:10:10.830 --> 00:10:12.160
yep

00:10:12.160 --> 00:10:15.790
And I hope this nation's
Superior is a mighty one.

00:10:15.790 --> 00:10:17.250
hype

00:10:25.830 --> 00:10:27.870
It's delicious! <i>Beyond</i> delicious!

00:10:27.870 --> 00:10:31.870
Did you come to Gideon to see
the Clash of the Superiors?

00:10:31.870 --> 00:10:34.000
Sure did, grizz!

00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:37.040
I'm here to see my pal Figgy fight.

00:10:37.040 --> 00:10:38.500
"Figgy"?

00:10:38.500 --> 00:10:42.080
Oh, Figaro. You're friends, huh?

00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:44.790
Is that what brought you here, too, grizz?

00:10:44.790 --> 00:10:45.870
Yeah.

00:10:47.870 --> 00:10:52.370
Ooh! Box seats, grizz!

00:10:52.370 --> 00:10:53.370
What's up?

00:10:53.370 --> 00:10:57.250
What a crazy coincidence:
We're in the same box, grizz.

00:10:57.250 --> 00:10:59.790
We can watch the fight together, grizz!

00:10:59.790 --> 00:11:02.040
So these things <i>do</i> happen!

00:11:02.040 --> 00:11:03.700
Listen, Ray...

00:11:03.700 --> 00:11:09.540
Judging by your gear, you must have done
a lot of adventuring in your short time here.

00:11:09.540 --> 00:11:15.620
It's not every day a player beats two
UBMs so soon after joining, grizz.

00:11:15.620 --> 00:11:19.250
Om-nom-nom. Gulp.

00:11:19.250 --> 00:11:26.450
Although Figgy and I beat our first UBM
when we were in our first low-rank jobs.

00:11:26.450 --> 00:11:32.660
We got lost in this one area and
wound up fighting two of the things.

00:11:32.660 --> 00:11:36.200
Two? So you and Figaro teamed up, two-on-two?

00:11:36.200 --> 00:11:40.620
No--we each took on one UBM alone. One on one.

00:11:40.620 --> 00:11:42.830
Shuichi joined the game on launch day--

00:11:42.830 --> 00:11:46.910
he must have been one of the first
Masters to take down a UBM.

00:11:46.910 --> 00:11:49.750
About how long do you spend
in <i>Dendro</i> on a given day?

00:11:49.750 --> 00:11:51.790
I make sure to play healthy!

00:11:51.790 --> 00:11:55.620
Can't go without my three squares,
baths, toilet breaks,

00:11:55.620 --> 00:11:58.950
and an hour-long workout to
keep up my muscles, grizz.

00:11:58.950 --> 00:12:02.660
So every other waking moment is spent here?!

00:12:02.660 --> 00:12:07.160
Oop--I've got someplace to be.
Catch you later, grizz.

00:12:07.160 --> 00:12:12.040
Can't wait to meet your buddy!

00:12:12.040 --> 00:12:14.870
What does Brother Bear do for a living?

00:12:14.870 --> 00:12:20.290
Oh, he won a huge overseas lottery,
bought some apartment buildings,

00:12:20.290 --> 00:12:21.040
--and has been retired and living easy
off the rent income ever since.

00:12:21.040 --> 00:12:24.580
--Ah... grizz.
--and has been retired and living easy
off the rent income ever since.

00:12:24.580 --> 00:12:28.080
My brother's background is all over the place.

00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:31.910
Just when he'd made it big as
a talented child actor and singer,

00:12:31.910 --> 00:12:35.500
he quit the entertainment industry
to become a martial artist.

00:12:35.500 --> 00:12:39.540
Then he became a university teaching assistant.

00:12:39.540 --> 00:12:42.830
That's all over the place, all right.

00:12:42.830 --> 00:12:44.250
Hmm?

00:12:46.540 --> 00:12:47.700
Delicious.

00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:50.540
Hey! That was my last bite!

00:12:50.540 --> 00:12:52.540
Gulp. Yoo-hoo.

00:12:52.540 --> 00:12:54.120
Hey, where's Hugo?

00:12:54.120 --> 00:12:56.040
He's coming.

00:12:59.200 --> 00:13:00.700
Hi, Ray!

00:13:00.700 --> 00:13:06.000
I suppose I have you and God
to thank for our safe reunion, eh?

00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:11.160
I should be thanking you, too.
There's something I wanted to discuss.

00:13:11.160 --> 00:13:16.080
I see! I had no idea the prize money
turned out to be quite so huge.

00:13:16.080 --> 00:13:18.290
And now we need to divvy it up.

00:13:18.290 --> 00:13:20.000
Count me out.

00:13:20.000 --> 00:13:23.160
Not a satisfactory answer, I see.

00:13:23.160 --> 00:13:26.200
Of course not! Let's split it
right down the middle.

00:13:26.200 --> 00:13:29.200
I'd be happy with half of that.

00:13:31.450 --> 00:13:33.290
Consider my share received.

00:13:33.290 --> 00:13:36.830
You're hardly greedy, are you, Ray?
You could have easily kept this from me.

00:13:36.830 --> 00:13:39.620
I would never lie to a friend!

00:13:43.120 --> 00:13:47.250
Hey, are you okay wandering
around in that getup?

00:13:47.250 --> 00:13:49.700
Isn't it the Dryfe army uniform?

00:13:49.700 --> 00:13:56.000
No, this is the Driver uniform for
my clan, the Triangle of Wisdom.

00:13:56.000 --> 00:13:59.080
Wearing it in this nation is no problem at all.

00:13:59.080 --> 00:14:04.790
Oh, okay. Why'd you go to
Dryfe in the first place?

00:14:04.790 --> 00:14:10.870
I knew someone there.
They got me into my clan as well.

00:14:10.870 --> 00:14:12.540
Ah, I get it.

00:14:12.540 --> 00:14:16.540
Now let me ask <i>you</i> something.

00:14:16.540 --> 00:14:20.250
Tell me all the details about yesterday's
battle against Gouz-Maise.

00:14:20.250 --> 00:14:22.540
Of course!

00:14:25.370 --> 00:14:27.700
It's about that time.

00:14:27.700 --> 00:14:29.040
Time for what?

00:14:29.040 --> 00:14:33.620
We're off to the arena to see
the Clash of Superiors.

00:14:33.620 --> 00:14:36.040
Are you going, too?

00:14:36.040 --> 00:14:38.580
Mmm, something like that.

00:14:38.580 --> 00:14:41.750
Well, maybe we'll see you there!

00:14:43.870 --> 00:14:46.580
See you again, Nemesis.

00:14:46.580 --> 00:14:49.660
Farewell for now, Cyco.

00:14:49.660 --> 00:14:50.370
Ray.

00:14:50.370 --> 00:14:52.000
Hmm? What's up?

00:14:52.000 --> 00:14:56.200
Something I'd like you to keep tucked
into a corner of your mind...

00:14:56.200 --> 00:14:58.370
It's west.

00:14:58.370 --> 00:14:59.700
"It"?

00:14:59.700 --> 00:15:03.450
It's no big deal. Just that
today's favorite, Figaro,

00:15:03.450 --> 00:15:06.910
is entering the arena from the west today.

00:15:06.910 --> 00:15:09.160
Oh, okay.

00:15:09.160 --> 00:15:11.580
See you later, Ray.

00:15:11.580 --> 00:15:14.040
Yep! See you, Hugo!

00:15:17.160 --> 00:15:21.870
Hugo, didn't you just leak information?

00:15:21.870 --> 00:15:23.250
Maybe so.

00:15:23.250 --> 00:15:26.830
Do you dislike our plan?

00:15:26.830 --> 00:15:32.700
I don't even know myself.
I want to fulfill his desires, of course...

00:15:32.700 --> 00:15:37.040
But at the same time,
I can't ignore a woman in distress.

00:15:37.040 --> 00:15:39.370
An antinomy.

00:15:39.370 --> 00:15:44.200
Which is why I told Ray. But that's all.

00:15:44.200 --> 00:15:46.500
I'll otherwise act according to plan.

00:15:46.500 --> 00:15:50.870
Then I will act alongside you.

00:15:50.870 --> 00:15:52.410
Thanks.

00:15:58.290 --> 00:16:01.250
I'm sorry, Master Xunyu.

00:16:01.250 --> 00:16:03.870
I wanted to go cheer you on...

00:16:05.040 --> 00:16:07.120
But it seems I can't.

00:16:07.120 --> 00:16:10.330
Don't force yourself. Take it easy; rest.

00:16:10.330 --> 00:16:14.120
Oh, dear... Shall I change
your ice pack, Your Highness?

00:16:14.120 --> 00:16:16.120
Or would you care for an apple?

00:16:16.120 --> 00:16:19.620
Master Xunyu, shouldn't you
be leaving for Gideon?

00:16:19.620 --> 00:16:22.790
Oh, will you look at the time...

00:16:24.160 --> 00:16:27.250
What's going on? Your Highness! Master Xunyu!

00:16:29.750 --> 00:16:33.120
Eh? Huh? H-Hey, um, Master Xunyu?

00:16:33.120 --> 00:16:36.830
Close the window after us.

00:16:36.830 --> 00:16:37.700
Huh?

00:16:37.700 --> 00:16:41.950
Well, ambassador, we're off to Gideon.

00:16:41.950 --> 00:16:43.620
Mind you don't bite your tongue.

00:16:43.620 --> 00:16:47.370
W-Wait, I'm not ready!

00:16:49.700 --> 00:16:54.160
Farewell, Master Xunyu... and Meihai!

00:16:54.160 --> 00:16:59.040
Hello there, Your Excellency.
We've had a change of plans.

00:16:59.040 --> 00:17:04.330
The first princess won't be coming,
so the Queen of Monsters won't make a move.

00:17:04.330 --> 00:17:08.750
I know, I know. She's the most
powerful in the Empire,

00:17:08.750 --> 00:17:11.790
so it makes a huge difference
if she's here or not.

00:17:11.790 --> 00:17:16.330
I mean, the three of us can still
take most of the battles.

00:17:16.330 --> 00:17:20.700
We've got those defectors, too.
I'd say a 90% chance of success.

00:17:20.700 --> 00:17:28.910
If there's a Superior we didn't plan on?
Mmm... maybe 50%.

00:17:29.830 --> 00:17:35.160
You thought it'd be lower?
Good one, Your Excellency!

00:17:35.160 --> 00:17:38.370
Did you forget who's here?

00:17:38.370 --> 00:17:44.040
We can handle a different target
or a little tweaking here and there.

00:17:44.040 --> 00:17:47.620
Just say a little prayer that we pull this off.

00:17:48.870 --> 00:17:53.700
She may not be here,
but I've still got my favorite.

00:17:53.700 --> 00:18:00.620
I wouldn't be surprised if his Embryo killed all
the Masters in Gideon all by himself.

00:18:03.120 --> 00:18:05.540
Blackwing Orchestra!

00:18:07.200 --> 00:18:10.620
World Reversal Waterfall!

00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:26.450
High-level stuff.

00:18:26.450 --> 00:18:27.290
Mmm-hmm.

00:18:27.290 --> 00:18:30.790
Both Masters have Sixth Form Embryos:

00:18:30.790 --> 00:18:36.950
Juliet the Fallen Knight
and Chelsea the Great Pirate.

00:18:36.950 --> 00:18:40.540
Wow, so she's in the knight grouping, huh?

00:18:40.540 --> 00:18:44.830
I do feel some closeness there,
but her gear looks pretty terrifying.

00:18:44.830 --> 00:18:48.160
You're one to talk.

00:18:48.160 --> 00:18:51.410
Ooh! She's going to finish this!

00:19:07.620 --> 00:19:09.450
Hræsvelgr!

00:19:11.830 --> 00:19:13.540
Poseidon!

00:19:17.120 --> 00:19:20.700
Those must be their ultimate skills,
named after their Embryos.

00:19:20.700 --> 00:19:21.950
Right.

00:19:21.950 --> 00:19:26.830
Hræsvelgr is a Dark-Wind combo magic attack.

00:19:26.830 --> 00:19:32.290
Poseidon is a physical attack
that summons molten gold.

00:19:42.370 --> 00:19:47.000
Amazing... so this is the power
of an ultimate skill!

00:19:47.950 --> 00:19:49.450
Is that...

00:19:49.450 --> 00:19:50.910
...my brother?

00:19:52.950 --> 00:19:55.660
Brother Bear isn't here.

00:19:55.660 --> 00:19:58.290
You'd think he'd stand out.

00:19:58.290 --> 00:20:03.000
That Caldina guy and Dryfe's
King of Beasts are in the audience.

00:20:03.000 --> 00:20:05.290
I've got their attention.

00:20:05.290 --> 00:20:08.500
Something's fishy in town, too.

00:20:08.500 --> 00:20:12.450
There's this suspicious bunch
that's supposedly with the kingdom--

00:20:12.450 --> 00:20:15.580
who knows what any of them
might have up their sleeve.

00:20:15.580 --> 00:20:17.290
Stay alert.

00:20:17.290 --> 00:20:19.450
I will.

00:20:19.450 --> 00:20:22.540
What is it? What's going on over--?

00:20:24.250 --> 00:20:25.330
Hey!

00:20:25.330 --> 00:20:28.370
Ah, Ray and Nemesis!

00:20:29.500 --> 00:20:32.830
Why the costume, Figaro?

00:20:32.830 --> 00:20:37.660
I'm well-known in this town, so I can't
walk around without a disguise.

00:20:37.660 --> 00:20:41.290
Aha. We had heard you two were friends;

00:20:41.290 --> 00:20:44.910
now I see you're close enough
to be cosplay pals.

00:20:44.910 --> 00:20:46.620
Friends, eh?

00:20:46.620 --> 00:20:48.620
Yes, I suppose so.

00:20:48.620 --> 00:20:51.660
You probably know that both Shu
and I are this nations' Su--

00:20:51.660 --> 00:20:56.450
...suavest representatives of
the Costume-Lovers' Club, grizz!

00:20:58.040 --> 00:21:03.040
Listen, I forgot to give you
something at lunch today, grizz.

00:21:03.040 --> 00:21:03.950
What's this?

00:21:03.950 --> 00:21:06.250
A Telepathy Cuff.

00:21:06.250 --> 00:21:10.200
Two friends with those equipped
can chat with each other, grizz.

00:21:10.200 --> 00:21:13.040
Wow, that sounds really handy!

00:21:13.040 --> 00:21:15.080
Oh, right--Ray?

00:21:15.080 --> 00:21:16.120
Yes?

00:21:16.120 --> 00:21:20.160
You should bet on me. You'll come out ahead.

00:21:20.160 --> 00:21:21.660
Got it.

00:21:21.660 --> 00:21:26.540
I'm gonna chat a little longer with
Figgy here, so you go on ahead, grizz.

00:21:26.540 --> 00:21:28.450
Okay, will do.

00:21:29.700 --> 00:21:33.250
Haven't you told him who you are?

00:21:33.250 --> 00:21:34.950
Never mind that.

00:21:34.950 --> 00:21:40.500
Look, you say you're going to win,
but from where I stand, the odds are 50/50.

00:21:40.500 --> 00:21:43.160
If not worse.

00:21:43.160 --> 00:21:45.830
That's how it looks from my end, too.

00:21:45.830 --> 00:21:50.700
After all, I'm facing one of the mighty
Huang He Si Ling--the empire's greatest four.

00:21:50.700 --> 00:21:56.120
Against the Kingdom of Altar's mightiest
solo player, Figaro the Endless Chain.

00:21:56.120 --> 00:22:00.160
What a match! I'd love to see it myself.

00:22:00.160 --> 00:22:01.660
Hey, now...

00:22:01.660 --> 00:22:03.790
Relax.

00:22:03.790 --> 00:22:09.290
These moments that set my life ablaze
are the whole reason I'm in <i>Infinite Dendrogram</i> .

00:22:09.290 --> 00:22:13.120
That's why I'll win this with all that I am.

00:23:44.410 --> 00:23:45.500
"Clash of the Superiors"

00:23:45.500 --> 00:23:47.410
"Clash of the Superiors"

00:23:45.500 --> 00:23:47.410
"Clash of the Superiors."

00:23:47.410 --> 00:23:48.370
"Clash of the Superiors"
